// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//
// Project-wide build settings that are a decision rather than a default.
// The project's Debug and Release configurations are based on this file,
// so every target inherits it; a target's own settings still win.

// One switch for the app group and the keychain group (Supporting/README.md).
//
// NO, the default: every target is standalone. No `application-groups` or
// `keychain-access-groups` entitlement, and `AlohaAppGroupEnabled` /
// `AlohaKeychainSharingEnabled` false in every Info.plist, so a free Apple ID
// can sign any target and CI (CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO) needs no profile. The
// cost: widgets, the share sheet, the notification service, complications
// and Top Shelf see no accounts, because each process has only its own
// container.
//
// YES: every target is entitled to `group.social.aloha.app` and
// `$(AppIdentifierPrefix)social.aloha.app` and says so in its Info.plist.
// Needs a team that has registered that group (or the identifiers changed to
// a group of your own).
//
// Debug is NO so anyone can build and run; Release is YES, because Release
// is what gets archived for the App Store and TestFlight, and a shipped build
// whose widgets, share sheet and Top Shelf see no accounts is broken. Only
// a team that owns the group can sign a Release build anyway; CI builds it
// with CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO, where entitlements are not applied.
//
// To change either, set it in Supporting/Local.xcconfig (git-ignored)
// rather than here:
//
//     ALOHA_SHARED_CONTAINER = YES
ALOHA_SHARED_CONTAINER = NO
ALOHA_SHARED_CONTAINER[config=Release] = YES

// What the switch selects. CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS names
// `<Target>$(ALOHA_ENTITLEMENTS_SUFFIX).entitlements`, and the Info.plists
// write `$(ALOHA_SHARED_CONTAINER)` into both keys, which `AppGroup` reads as
// a boolean. Anything but YES is treated as NO.
ALOHA_ENTITLEMENTS_SUFFIX_YES = -Shared
ALOHA_ENTITLEMENTS_SUFFIX = $(ALOHA_ENTITLEMENTS_SUFFIX_$(ALOHA_SHARED_CONTAINER))

// A contributor's own overrides, never committed. Optional: the build does
// not need the file to exist.
#include? "Local.xcconfig"
